blocks.body:
The radius gives the open interval (c − R, c + R). To get the interval of CONVERGENCE, substitute x = c − R and x = c + R in turn and test each resulting numerical series. There are only three outcomes, and all three occur in this lesson's examples:
  both endpoints diverge → open interval, as for Σ(x+3)ⁿ/2ⁿ on (−5, −1);
  one converges → half-open, as for Σ(x−2)ⁿ/n on [1, 3);
  both converge → closed, as for Σ|x−5|ⁿ/((n+1)(n+2)) on [4, 6].
